The portable C in the scenario mouse-list: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/mouse-list.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 10 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the mouse's pointer is on the first cell of the screen, on the first
letter of the banner, which is V in the portable C. The rule of the name
leaves a cell in another colour as the original has it, and the pointer
turns the colours of its cell round: so the row with - has the original's T
in front of the portable C's line

